# vergeio_network_dns_record (Resource)

`vergeio_network_dns_record` is one record in a [`vergeio_network_dns_zone`](network_dns_zone.md). Set `zone_id` to that zone id so Terraform destroys this record before the zone.

`value` is the record data. For an A or AAAA record, set `value` to `vergeio_vm_nic.example.ipaddress` so the VM and the record live in one module. Or set `vm_nic_id` to that NIC id and leave `value` unset. Terraform reads the NIC address and writes it. A later plan updates the record when the NIC address changes. Do not set both.

`apply` defaults to true and refreshes DNS on the zone network after a change. Set `apply` to false on the view and the zone, and leave it true on this record with `depends_on` those two, so DNS reloads once. A stopped network is not refreshed. It loads staged DNS when it starts.

